    "done_when": "E101011's G-EQDSK is copied once, read-only, from /home/d240034/fbequ/EFIT95.DATA on the JT-60SA host (nakasvr26, the one ssh connection the copy needs, reading nothing else there) to /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101011.geqdsk, its sha256 recorded in the fragment. E101011's plasma current, loop 7 (MDAC magFlxLp7) and TF coil current are cached through fetch_channels in one more ssh connection, refetching nothing cached. A loader in imas_ambix/challenge/loader.py, the owner of EfitLabels, reads a G-EQDSK through the eqdsk package's EQDSKInterface.from_file into an EfitLabels record (psirz, grids, boundary, axis, q95, vacuum field),. eqdsk is imported as installed through torax and not yet declared directly; the fragment lists that declaration as a follow-on. scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py adds E101011 as a row whose equilibrium half is that record. The regenerated report scores the poloidal-flux relation and the declared flux exponent on that row, states whether the file's psi is per radian (e_Bp = 0) and which candidates then survive, and keeps the decision jt60sa-source-cocos scope: it settles SELENE's output COCOS, and the diagnostics' flux and current signs stay confirmed per channel. New tests in tests/challenge/test_loader.py read a small G-EQDSK written under tmp_path into EfitLabels; tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py gains a row with a flux half alongside the FAME rows. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset and the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/challenge/test_loader.py tests/challenge/test_convention.py tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py; it exits 0, the cohort script exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Write the manifest before any long wait. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
